## 🚀 About

MedTwin-AI is a full-stack machine learning web application that predicts a patient’s health risk using key vital parameters such as age, heart rate, blood pressure, oxygen level (SpO₂), and blood sugar.

The system combines a Decision Tree-based machine learning model with a rule-based health scoring engine to provide both predictions and clear explanations.

The goal of this project is to demonstrate how AI can be applied to real-world healthcare scenarios in a simple, interpretable, and user-friendly way.

---

## ✨ Key Features

- 🧠 ML-based risk prediction (Low / Moderate / High)
- 🌳 Decision Tree model for interpretable decisions
- 📊 Probability visualization using Chart.js
- 📈 Health score with grading system
- 💡 Explainable AI (reasons + feature contributions)
- ⚡ Real-time predictions via web interface
- 🎨 Clean and modern UI with animations

---

## 🛠️ Tech Stack

- Language: Python  
- Backend: Flask  
- Machine Learning: Scikit-learn (DecisionTreeClassifier)  
- Libraries: NumPy  
- Frontend: HTML, CSS, JavaScript  
- Visualization: Chart.js  

---

## 🧠 System Architecture

User Input  
↓  
Flask Backend  
↓  
Decision Tree Model  
↓  
Health Score Engine  
↓  
Result + Visualization UI  

---

## 🧠 How It Works

1. User enters health data via the web interface  
2. Flask backend receives and processes the input  
3. Data is passed to the trained Decision Tree model  
4. Model predicts the risk level along with probabilities  
5. A rule-based engine calculates the health score and grade  
6. Results are displayed with visual charts and explanations  

---

## 📂 Project Structure

MedTwin-AI/
│  
├── main.py              # Flask backend  
├── model.py             # ML model (Decision Tree)  
├── health_score.py      # Scoring + explanation logic  
├── requirements.txt  
│  
├── templates/  
│   ├── index.html       # Input page  
│   └── result.html      # Result page  

